 /*
- * Compile-only groundwork for the Apple T7000-family PCIe host controller.
+ * Apple T7000-family PCIe host controller -- link/enumeration test driver.
  *
- * The real J81 ADT describes four ports, four port interrupts and twelve
- * register windows. Corellium's older H9P driver confirms the four-port
- * controller shape, but its register layout, SART and hard-coded PHY sequence
- * are not valid for T7000. The disabled device tree preserves J81's exact
- * resource ordering without naming the unresolved small-window roles. Keep
- * this driver inert until those roles, DART attachment and ADT-provided
- * tunables have been implemented.
+ * Deliberately bounded to the smallest useful test: bring up port 1 (the
+ * only populated port on J81/BCM4350), then let the generic PCI/ECAM core
+ * scan the bus and report the result through its own standard sysfs/dmesg
+ * output (vendor/device/revision IDs). No brcmfmac, no firmware upload, no
+ * WiFi association, no touching ports 2-4.
+ *
+ * Register offsets, bit positions and the two microsecond delays below are
+ * traced directly from AppleT7000PCIe::_enablePortHardware and
+ * AppleEmbeddedPCIEPort::enableGated in the real J81 iOS 8.1 kernelcache --
+ * not guessed. See docs/plans/2026-09-13-j81-wifi-pcie.md's "Enable-sequence
+ * checkpoint" and "port enable order" sections for the full evidence trail.
+ * Register windows 2/4/6/8 (of the ADT's 12 total) are confirmed unused by
+ * Apple's own host path and are intentionally left unmapped. CLKREQ is
+ * confirmed endpoint/controller-managed and is not toggled here. PERST# is
+ * not hand-rolled either -- the DT's port-1 child node carries a standard
+ * "reset-gpios" property, which pci_host_common_init()'s own
+ * pci_host_common_parse_ports()/pci_host_probe() path already deasserts at
+ * the right point in its own sequence.
  */

